With the ability to execute arbitrary commands the malware is essentially infinitely extensively and gives a remote attacker full control over the infected system.
The malware can also interact with the UI, for example to capture a screen shot. When the malware receives “command” 0x37
(55d
), it invokes the CGMainDisplayID
and CGDisplayCreateImage
to create an image of the user’s desktop:
0x0000622c movss dword [esp+0x34ac+var_101C], xmm0
